</math> each time <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> increases by <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>. Since the function <math alttext="upper E left parenthesis t right parenthesis equals 5 left parenthesis 1.8 right parenthesis Superscript t"><mi>E</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.8</mn></mfenced><mi>t</mi></msup></math> gives the estimated number of employees at a restaurant and <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> is the number of years since the restaurant opened, the best interpretation of the number <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math> in this context is the estimated number of employees when <math alttext="t equals 0"><mrow>
	<mi>t</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
