    ($SATQ$be1b8c74$SATQ$, $SATQ$a1e6d838-3642-4546-9031-e113b254b3f2$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables $SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="x equals 8 a left parenthesis b plus 9 right parenthesis"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>
<p>The given equation relates the positive numbers <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math>, <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math>, and <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>. Which equation correctly expresses <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> in terms of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"96630b2c-7929-4dc5-9402-33c10abc522b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction x Over 8 EndFraction minus left parenthesis b plus 9 right parenthesis\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"f0dca31b-2a55-4481-ab9a-fcb5012170ad","content":"<p><math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction x Over 8 left parenthesis b plus 9 right parenthesis EndFraction\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"ba9adc01-ab7a-45b7-82f3-da78f79d22ea","content":"<p><math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction 8 left parenthesis b plus 9 right parenthesis Over x EndFraction\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"da03ff0f-c653-4e1d-95e8-2b42952de2ac","content":"<p><math alttext=\"a equals 8 x left parenthesis b plus 9 right parenthesis\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["f0dca31b-2a55-4481-ab9a-fcb5012170ad"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. To express <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> in terms of <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>, the given equation can be rewritten such that <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> is isolated on one side of the equation. Since it&rsquo;s given that <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> is a positive number, <math alttext="b plus 9"><mrow>
	<mi>b</mi>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mn>9</mn>
</mrow>
</math> is not equal to zero. Therefore, dividing both sides of the given equation by <math alttext="8 left parenthesis b plus 9 right parenthesis"><mn>8</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;yields the equivalent equation <math alttext="StartFraction x Over 8 left parenthesis b plus 9 right parenthesis EndFraction equals a"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math>, or <math alttext="a equals StartFraction x Over 8 left parenthesis b plus 9 right parenthesis EndFraction"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This equation is equivalent to <math alttext="x equals 8 left parenthesis a plus left parenthesis b plus 9 right parenthesis right parenthesis"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>
