</math>, in the given function.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"beca03de","external_id":"abfd9618-c65d-4fd8-9f89-254e3dfa9529","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"0c58debc-d6a4-4e07-ad16-ad1465146362","uId":"00e83679-c3d7-4a99-a021-2eb49c3891b2","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A rectangle has a length that is <math alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn>\n</math> times its width. The function <math alttext=\"y equals left parenthesis 15 w right parenthesis left parenthesis w right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mi>w</mi></mfenced></math> represents this situation, where <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is the area, in square feet, of the rectangle and <math alttext=\"y greater than 0\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Which of the following is the best interpretation of <math alttext=\"15 w\"><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow><mi>w</mi></math> in this context?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"bc6bd898-a4f3-455d-b693-5639f13afc68","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length of the rectangle, in feet</p>"},{"id":"f34d15cf-ad03-47dd-8464-32dcdb4882af","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The area of the rectangle, in square feet</p>"},{"id":"6584dd8c-97db-4b76-bb2a-e86b63e23b98","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The difference between the length and the width of the rectangle, in feet</p>"},{"id":"a28c9227-fcb1-4b55-b26d-721b54ece582","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">&nbsp;The width of the rectangle, in feet</p>"}],"keys":["bc6bd898-a4f3-455d-b693-5639f13afc68"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It's 