_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","createDate":1691007959826,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":null,"external_id":"abfd9618-c65d-4fd8-9f89-254e3dfa9529","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"00e83679-c3d7-4a99-a021-2eb49c3891b2","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"keys":["bc6bd898-a4f3-455d-b693-5639f13afc68"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It's given that a rectangle has a length that is <math alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn>\n</math> times its width. It's also given that the function <math alttext=\"y equals left parenthesis 15 w right parenthesis left parenthesis w right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>15</mn><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mi>w</mi></mfenced></math> represents this situation, where <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is the area, in square feet, of the rectangle and <math alttext=\"y greater than 0\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. The area of a rectangle can be calculated by multiplying the rectangle's length by its width. Since the rectangle has a length that is <math alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn>\n</math> times its width, it follows that <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> represents the width of the rectangle, in feet, and <math alttext=\"15 w\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>15</mn>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> represents the length of the rectangle, in feet. Therefore, the best interpretation of <math alttext=\"15 w\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>15</mn>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> in this context is that it's the length of the rectangle, in feet.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the best interpretation of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"15 w\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>15</mn>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, in the given function.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the best interpretation of <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"15 w\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>15</mn>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, in the given function.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A rectangle has a length that is <math alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn>\n</math> times its width. The function <math alttext=\"y equals left parenthesis 15 w right parenthesis left parenthesis w right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mi>w</mi></mfenced></math> represents this situation, where <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is the area, in square feet, of the rectangle and <math alttext=\"y greater than 0\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Which of the following is the best interpretation of <math alttext=\"15 w\"><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow><mi>w</mi></math> in this context?</p>","externalid":"abfd9618-c65d-4fd8-9f89-254e3dfa9529","templateid":"4cf25842-b848-4b99-ad35-0ef4b580aa49","vaultid":"0c58debc-d6a4-4e07-ad16-ad1465146362","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"bc6bd898-a4f3-455d-b693-5639f13afc68","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length of the rectangle, in feet</p>"},{"id":"f34d15cf-ad03-47dd-8464-32dcdb4882af","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The area of the rectangle, in square feet</p>"},{"id":"6584dd8c-97db-4b76-bb2a-e86b63e23b98","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The difference between the length and the width of the rectangle, in feet</p>"},{"id":"a28c9227-fcb1-4b55-b26d-721b54ece582","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">&nbsp;The width of the rectangle, in feet</p>"}],"correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1691007959826,"updateDate":1691007959826}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959826, 1691007959826),
    ($SATQ$bef4b1c6$SATQ$, $SATQ$f70845bb-9302-4075-b020-3ece6ab22306$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$4878d098-80a0-417a-9f51-59a956767076$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables $SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="StartFraction 55 Over x plus 6 EndFraction equals x"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mfrac>
			<mn>55</mn>
			<mrow>
				<mi>x</mi>
				<mo>+</mo>
				<mn>6</mn>
			</mrow>
		</mfrac>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">What is the positive solution to the given equation?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math>. Multiplying both sides of the given equation by <math alttext="x plus 6"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mn>6</mn>
</mrow>
</math> results in <math alttext="55 equals x left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis"><mn>55</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Applying the distributive property of multiplication to the right-hand side of this equation results in <math alttext="55 equals x squared plus 6 x"><mrow>
	<mn>55</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<msup>
			<mi>x</mi>
			<mn>2</mn>
		</msup>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mrow>
			<mn>6</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="55"><mn>55</mn>
</math> from both sides of this equation results in <math alttext="0 equals x squared plus 6 x minus 55"><mrow>
	<mn>0</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<msup>
			<mi>x</mi>
			<mn>2</mn>
		</msup>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mrow>
			<mn>6</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>55</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. The right-hand side of this equation can be rewritten by factoring. The two values that multiply to <math alttext="negative 55"><mo>-</mo><mn>55</mn>
</math> and add to <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> are <math alttext="11"><mn>11</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="negative 5"><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn>
</math>. It follows that the equation <math alttext="0 equals x squared plus 6 x minus 55"><mrow>
	<mn>0</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<msup>
			<mi>x</mi>
			<mn>2</mn>
		</msup>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mrow>
			<mn>6</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>55</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> can be rewritten as <math alttext="0 equals left parenthesis x plus 11 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 5 right parenthesis"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Setting each factor equal to <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math> yields two equations: <math alttext="x plus 11 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>11</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math> and <math alttext="x minus 5 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>5</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="11"><mn>11</mn>
</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext="x plus 11 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>11</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math> results in <math alttext="x equals negative 11"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Adding <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math> to both sides of the equation <math alttext="x minus 5 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>5</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math> results in <math alttext="x equals 5"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>5</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the positive solution to the given equation is <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"bef4b1c6","external_id":"f70845bb-9302-4075-b020-3ece6ab22306","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"4878d098-80a0-417a-9f51-59a956767076","uId":"ca041044-8afe-4361-91b7-3cb54b318d2f","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"StartFraction 55 Over x plus 6 EndFraction equals x\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<mn>55</mn>\n\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">What is the positive solution to the given equation?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["5"],"correct_answer":["5"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math>. Multiplying both sides of the given equation by <math alttext=\"x plus 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> results in <math alttext=\"55 equals x left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis\"><mn>55</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Applying the distributive property of multiplication to the right-hand side of this equation results in <math alttext=\"55 equals x squared plus 6 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>55</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"55\"><mn>55</mn>\n</math> from both sides of this equation results in <math alttext=\"0 equals x squared plus 6 x minus 55\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>55</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. The right-hand side of this equation can be rewritten by factoring. The two values that multiply to <math alttext=\"negative 55\"><mo>-</mo><mn>55</mn>\n</math> and add to <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> are <math alttext=\"11\"><mn>11</mn>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"negative 5\"><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn>\n</math>. It follows that the equation <math alttext=\"0 equals x squared plus 6 x minus 55\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>55</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x plus 11 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 5 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Setting each factor equal to <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math> yields two equations: <math alttext=\"x plus 11 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>11</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"x minus 5 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"11\"><mn>11</mn>\n</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x plus 11 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>11</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> results in <math alttext=\"x equals negative 11\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Adding <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math> to both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x minus 5 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> results in <math alttext=\"x equals 5\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>5</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the positive solution to the given equation is <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959823,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"bef4b1c6","skill_cd":"P.B.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","createDate":1691007959823,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":null,"external_id":"f70845bb-9302-4075-b020-3ece6ab22306","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"ca041044-8afe-4361-91b7-3cb54b318d2f","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"keys":["5"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math>. Multiplying both sides of the given equation by <math alttext=\"x plus 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> results in <math alttext=\"55 equals x left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis\"><mn>55</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Applying the distributive property of multiplication to the right-hand side of this equation results in <math alttext=\"55 equals x squared plus 6 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>55</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"55\"><mn>55</mn>\n</math> from both sides of this equation results in <math alttext=\"0 equals x squared plus 6 x minus 55\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>55</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. The right-hand side of this equation can be rewritten by factoring. The two values that multiply to <math alttext=\"negative 55\"><mo>-</mo><mn>55</mn>\n</math> and add to <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> are <math alttext=\"11\"><mn>11</mn>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"negative 5\"><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn>\n</math>. It follows that the equation <math alttext=\"0 equals x squared plus 6 x minus 55\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>55</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x plus 11 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 5 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Setting each factor equal to <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math> yields two equations: <math alttext=\"x plus 11 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>11</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"x minus 5 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"11\"><mn>11</mn>\n</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x plus 11 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>11</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> results in <math alttext=\"x equals negative 11\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Adding <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math> to both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x minus 5 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> results in <math alttext=\"x equals 5\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>5</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the positive solution to the given equation is <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math>.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"StartFraction 55 Over x plus 6 EndFraction equals x\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<mn>55</mn>\n\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">What is the positive solution to the given equation?</p>","externalid":"f70845bb-9302-4075-b020-3ece6ab22306","templateid":"a1db9297-1726-423a-95d8-842929adbac3","vaultid":"4878d098-80a0-417a-9f51-59a956767076","type":"spr","answerOptions":[],"correct_answer":["5"]},"createDate":1691007959823,"updateDate":1691007959823}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959823, 1691007959823),
