le=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c3a72da5/img_002_abaf44db.png\" alt=\"12 x to the fourth power, plus 14 x cubed\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c3a72da5/img_003_030d9961.png\" alt=\"7 x to the fourth power, plus 9 x cubed\"></span></span></p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. Adding the two expressions yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c3a72da5/img_006_42ecff90.png\" alt=\"3 x to the fourth power, plus 2 x to the third power, plus 4 x to the fourth power, plus 7 x to the third power\"></span>. Because the pair of terms <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c3a72da5/img_007_54b064a7.png\" alt=\"3 x to the fourth power \"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c3a72da5/img_008_1eee0bd6.png\" alt=\"4 x to the fourth power\"></span> and the pair of terms <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c3a72da5/img_009_2f4f91df.png\" alt=\"2 x to the third power \"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c3a72da5/img_010_e19187cc.png\" alt=\"7 x to the third power \"></span> each contain the same variable raised to the same power, they are like terms and can be combined as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c3a72da5/img_011_bd57c2dc.png\" alt=\"7 x to the fourth power \"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c3a72da5/img_012_6b1298bf.png\" alt=\"9 x to the third power\"></span>, respectively. The sum of the given expressions therefore simplifies to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/c3a72da5/img_013_030d9961.png\" alt=\"7 x to the fourth power, plus 9 x to the third power\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from adding the coefficients and the exponents in the given expressions. Choice B is incorrect and may result from adding the exponents as well as the coefficients of the like terms in the given expressions. Choice C is incorrect and may result from multiplying, rather than adding, the coefficients of the like terms in the given expressions.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":14,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959625,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"c3a72da5","skill_cd":"P.A.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","createDate":1691007959625,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"029468-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"bf251f6b-7de1-4dc7-a141-15f0e5196708","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"029468-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Which of the following is equivalent to the sum of <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 x to the fourth power, plus 2 x cubed\"></span></span> and <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"4 x to the fourth power, plus 7 x cubed\"></span></span>?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"16 x to the fourteenth power\"></span></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"7 x to the eighth power, plus 9 x to the sixth power\"></span></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"12 x to the fourth power, plus 14 x cubed\"></span></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"7 x to the fourth power, plus 9 x cubed\"></span></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"d","rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. Adding the two expressions yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 x to the fourth power, plus 2 x to the third power, plus 4 x to the fourth power, plus 7 x to the third power\"></span>. Because the pair of terms <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 x to the fourth power \"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"4 x to the fourth power\"></span> and the pair of terms <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x to the third power \"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"7 x to the third power \"></span> each contain the same variable raised to the same power, they are like terms and can be combined as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"7 x to the fourth power \"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"9 x to the third power\"></span>, respectively. The sum of the given expressions therefore simplifies to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"7 x to the fourth power, plus 9 x to the third power\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from adding the coefficients and the exponents in the given expressions. Choice B is incorrect and may result from adding the exponents as well as the coefficients of the like terms in the given expressions. Choice C is incorrect and may result from multiplying, rather than adding, the coefficients of the like terms in the given expressions.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959625,"updateDate":1691007959625}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959625, 1691007959625),
    ($SATQ$c3b116d7$SATQ$, $SATQ$77bede4f-84ec-4063-9b73-a0d1bd0cff6b$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$6cf879f5-7b74-4fa8-869b-7b65173aab84$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Equivalent expressions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Which of the following expressions is(are) a factor of <math alttext="3 x squared plus 20 x minus 63"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>3</mn>
		<msup>
			<mi>x</mi>
			<mn>2</mn>
		</msup>
	</mrow>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mn>20</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>-</mo>
	<mn>63</mn>
</mrow>
</math>?</p>
<ol style="list-style-type: upper-roman;">
<li>&nbsp;<math alttext="x minus 9"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>-</mo>
	<mn>9</mn>
</mrow>
</math></li>
<li><math alttext="3 x minus 7"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>3</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>-</mo>
	<mn>7</mn>
</mrow>
</math></li>
</ol>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"1276b973-e966-4c71-b6e5-368ac3352e34","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">I only</p>"},{"id":"30ebd9a3-a9c0-40d6-beeb-4298368146c4","content":"<p>II only</p>"},{"id":"f2497d8c-a1ab-49db-b014-7717d1abd0fe","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">I and II</p>"},{"id":"c59f6db9-d526-477c-b132-21348f7bad2c","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Neither I nor II</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["30ebd9a3-a9c0-40d6-beeb-4298368146c4"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. The given expression can be factored by first finding two values whose sum is <math alttext="20"><mn>20</mn>
</math> and whose product is <math alttext="3 left parenthesis negative 63 right parenthesis"><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>63</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="negative 189"><mo>-</mo><mn>189</mn>
</math>. Those two values are <math alttext="27"><mn>27</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="negative 7"><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn>
</math>. It follows that the given expression can be rewritten as <math alttext="3 x squared plus 27 x minus 7 x minus 63"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>27</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>63</mn></math>. Since the first two terms of this expression have a common factor of <math alttext="3 x"><mrow>
	<mn>3</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> and the last two terms of this expression have a common factor of <math alttext="negative 7"><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn>
</math>, this expression can be rewritten as <math alttext="3 x left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis minus 7 left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Since the two terms of this expression have a common factor of <math alttext="left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, it can be rewritten as <math alttext="left parenthesis 3 x minus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Therefore, expression II,&nbsp;<math alttext="3 x minus 7"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></math>, is a factor of <math alttext="3 x squared plus 20 x minus 63"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>63</mn></math>, but expression I,&nbsp;<math alttext="x minus 9"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math>, is not a factor of <math alttext="3 x squared plus 20 x minus 63"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>63</mn></math>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"c3b116d7","external_id":"77bede4f-84ec-4063-9b73-a0d1bd0cff6b","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"6cf879f5-7b74-4fa8-869b-7b65173aab84","uId":"14c4f302-14cc-4bd0-b52a-ff9ee5ef96ec","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.A.","skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which of the following expressions is(are) a factor of <math alttext=\"3 x squared plus 20 x minus 63\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>20</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>63</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>?</p>\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-roman;\">\n<li>&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x minus 9\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>9</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></li>\n<li><math alttext=\"3 x minus 7\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>7</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></li>\n</ol>","answerOptions":[{"id":"1276b973-e966-4c71-b6e5-368ac3352e34","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">I only</p>"},{"id":"30ebd9a3-a9c0-40d6-beeb-4298368146c4","content":"<p>II only</p>"},{"id":"f2497d8c-a1ab-49db-b014-7717d1abd0fe","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">I and II</p>"},{"id":"c59f6db9-d526-477c-b132-21348f7bad2c","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Neither I nor II</p>"}],"keys":["30ebd9a3-a9c0-40d6-beeb-4298368146c4"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The given expression can be factored by first finding two values whose sum is <math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math> and whose product is <math alttext=\"3 left parenthesis negative 63 right pare